{:edb/db-before-t 2094 :edb/db-after-t 2095 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535407 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:31:26.391Z" 13194139535407 true] [17592186347614 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347615 13194139535407 false] [17592186347614 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347719 13194139535407 true] [17592186347614 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 2z}.\n$$" 13194139535407 false] [17592186347614 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 2z}.\n$$\n\nInterpret the unchanged inequalities in real coordinates. The square root requires $2-x^2\\ge0$, so the actual nonempty $x$ projection is $[-\\sqrt2,\\sqrt2]$. Find the volume using this real domain." 13194139535407 true] [17592186347614 1145 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{2z}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}2z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[{z}^{2}]}_{z=-0}^{z=\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{(\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}})}^{2}-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}2-{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[2x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=-2}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(2(2)-\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3})-(2(-2)-\\frac{1}{3}(-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =(4-\\frac{8}{3})-(-4+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535407 false] [17592186347614 1145 "The inequalities defining $R$ are retained exactly. In real coordinates, $\\sqrt{2-x^2}$ is defined only for $|x|\\le\\sqrt2$. These values also satisfy the printed nominal bound $-2\\le x\\le2$. Thus the actual real solid is equivalently\n\n$$R=\\{(x,y,z):-\\sqrt2\\le x\\le\\sqrt2,\\ 0\\le z\\le\\sqrt{2-x^2},\\ 0\\le y\\le2z\\}.$$\n\nIts volume is\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\nV&=\\int_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2-x^2}}\\int_0^{2z}1\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\\\\\n&=\\int_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2-x^2}}2z\\,dz\\,dx\\\\\n&=\\int_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}(2-x^2)\\,dx\n=\\left[2x-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}\n=\\frac{8\\sqrt2}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe original source accepted $8/3$. That value is the ordinary signed polynomial integral $\\int_{-2}^{2}(2-x^2)\\,dx$. It does not give the volume of this real solid: the source square-root bounds are undefined for $\\sqrt2<|x|\\le2$. All five original choices are retained as alternatives, and $8\\sqrt2/3$ is added as the correct study answer." 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347616 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347617 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347618 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347619 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347620 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347720 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1041 "selection" 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347720 13194139535407 true] [17592186347719 1110 #uuid "540253a4-0f46-5ab3-a0e1-e391550ba551" 13194139535407 true] [17592186347720 1034 "\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{3}" 13194139535407 true] [17592186347720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535407 true] [17592186347720 1111 #uuid "72e6b0d3-28f5-5f08-ba4c-ac570bdbafae" 13194139535407 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-161659/real-volume-v1/selection" 17592186347719 "q-161659/real-volume-v1/selection/answer-8sqrt2-3" 17592186347720} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
